{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#151","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#151","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#151\",\"parent_revision\":\"dbc90cb07f0b914288c20a7f08cf475060c95dba346195713a6338c00a95ebb3\",\"root_revision\":\"dbc90cb07f0b914288c20a7f08cf475060c95dba346195713a6338c00a95ebb3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#147 fixed `AgentFrontmatter.skills`, which was typed `str | None` with a `normalize_comma_separated` validator that flattened a YAML list into a CSV string. `SkillFrontmatter.skills` still has exactly that shape.\\n\\nTwo separate questions follow, and they should be answered in order:\\n\\n**1. Is `skills` a `SKILL.md` field at all?** The AgentSkills specification defines six frontmatter fields for `SKILL.md`: `name`, `description`, `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, `allowed-tools`. `skills` is not among them \u2014 it is documented as *subagent* frontmatter (`sub-agents.md`). FM008 was deleted in #105 for precisely this reason: it asserted a `skills` shape on `SKILL.md`, where the field is not defined.\\n\\nIf `skills` is not a `SKILL.md` field, `SkillFrontmatter.skills` is modelling something the spec does not describe, and the fix is removal rather than retyping.\\n\\n**2. If it is retained, the CSV coercion is still wrong.** It silently rewrites a list into a string, which is the same class of silent mutation as #114 and the reason #147 removed the coercion on the agent side.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Is Separate From 147\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#147's scope named `AgentFrontmatter.skills` only, and `SkillFrontmatter.skills` remains load-bearing for the `--fix` restore guard in `plugin_validator._normalize_tool_fields_and_detect_changes`. Changing it without first answering question 1 risks breaking that guard for the file type where it still does work.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #147 \u2014 fixed the agent-side model\\n- #105 \u2014 deleted FM008 and the evidence behind it\\n- #114 \u2014 silent `--fix` mutation, same class\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bf4d35b0c50a024d7da81bcc74f49fb425522428544c68718eb8f433dcc74ed6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-UTA\"}"}